// expect-error: never given a backing store
//
// An `Arena` with no backing store has capacity 0, so EVERY alloc() returns
// null — forever. Before 2026-08-20 that compiled with no diagnostic at either
// end and produced no crash: the null just flows into the caller's `orelse`
// path and the program quietly does nothing. Silent on hosted and on bare metal
// alike, which is the class ZER refuses to ship.
//
// It also generated vacuous tests. `orelse return` in a `u32 main()` returns 0
// — PASS — so tests/zer/super_freelist_arena.zer reported success after
// executing four of its ~120 lines, with the freelist it exists to test never
// running. That file was the ONLY corpus casualty of this rule.
struct Block { u32 data; }

Arena scratch;          // declared, never given a backing store

u32 main() {
    *Block b = scratch.alloc(Block) orelse { return 1; };
    b.data = 7;
    return 0;
}
